From: Omarchy Mobile <omamobile@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom-smbchg: terminate and recharge on the charger's own sensing

smbchg_init() points the charger's termination current and recharge
voltage readings at the fuel gauge. Those sources only work once the fuel
gauge is set up for them, and pmi8994_fg doesn't do that.

On a Redmi 4 Prime (PMI8950, msm8953-xiaomi-markw) charging therefore
never terminated. The charger tapered at 4.368 V with the battery taking
147 mA, below the 300 mA termination current, and no charge-done
interrupt (chg-tcc-thr) came in 19 h or since. It tapered on until the
battery overvoltage comparator tripped (BAT_IF RT_STS bit 4, batt-ov) and
chg-error latched. Charging then stayed stopped with the battery near
4.20 V, at about 90 %, and each error also dropped the USB role to none.

Use the charger's analog sensing for both, so it terminates at its own
termination current and recharges 100 mV below the float voltage.

---
 drivers/power/supply/qcom-smbchg.c | 13 ++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom-smbchg.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom-smbchg.c
@@ -1470,13 +1470,20 @@
 
 	/*
 	 * Charger configuration, part 1:
-	 * - Set recharge voltage reading source to fuel gauge
-	 * - Set charge termination current reading source to fuel gauge
+	 * - Set recharge voltage reading source to the charger's own sensing
+	 * - Set charge termination current reading source to the charger's
+	 *   own sensing
+	 *
+	 * The fuel gauge sources need the fuel gauge to be programmed for
+	 * them, which pmi8994_fg does not do. With them, charging never terminated:
+	 * it tapered on below the termination current until the battery
+	 * overvoltage comparator tripped, and then stopped in an error state
+	 * that nothing cleared.
 	 */
 	ret = qcom_pmic_sec_masked_write(
 		chip->regmap, chip->base + SMBCHG_CHGR_CHGR_CFG1,
 		RECHG_THRESHOLD_SRC_BIT | TERM_I_SRC_BIT,
-		RCHG_SRC_FG | TERM_SRC_FG);
+		RCHG_SRC_ANA | TERM_SRC_ANA);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
